    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253">

                <pb facs="0499" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg451"/>

                <head>No. 253.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Moran.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 28,
                        1876</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 62.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of a letter of the
                    Secretary of the Navy, dated the 18th instant, in which he suggests the
                    desirability of the co-operation of the Governments of Portugal and Brazil in
                    the determination, telegraphically from Paris, of the longitudes of both coasts
                    of South America.</p>
                <p>You are requested to present the suggestion of the Navy Department to the
                    Government of Portugal, and to inform me of its reply at your early
                    convenience.</p>
                <p>An instruction similar to this will be addressed to the minister at Bio de
                    Janeiro.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d253-a1.xml" xpointer="d253-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
